The question here is the SAME as the aliens taxonomy. The question is NOT do cryptids exist. The question IS WHY ARE THEY NEARLY 100% BIPEDIAL CREATURES!

OK Here are the cryptids:

Hominids & Primates (Yeti-like):
-Bigfoot (Sasquatch): Large, ape-like hominid primarily reported in the Pacific Northwest forests of North America.
- Yeti (Abominable Snowman): High-altitude, white-furred hominid native to the Himalayan region of Asia.
- Yeren: Reddish-furred, bipedal primate reported in the remote mountains of Hubei Province, China.
- Yowie: Tall, aggressive bipedal ape-man from the Australian outback and temperate forests.
- Almas: Wild, human-like cryptid tracking through the Caucasus and Pamir Mountains of Central Asia.
- Maricoxi: Giant, aggressive ape-men reported by explorer Percy Fawcett in the Amazon rainforest.
- Agogwe: Small, woolly, bipedal humanoid sighted in the forests of East Africa.
- Batutut: Hairy, bipedal hominid closely resembling Bigfoot, reported in the dense jungles of Vietnam.
- Orang Pendek: Short, ground-dwelling, bipedal primate documented in the remote rainforests of Sumatra.

Lacustrine & Marine Monsters (Water-dwelling):
- Loch Ness Monster ("Nessie"): Long-necked aquatic creature infamously reported in Loch Ness, Scotland.
- Champ: Plesiosaur-like lake monster sighted frequently in Lake Champlain, North America.
- Ogopogo: Serpentine aquatic cryptid residing in Okanagan Lake, British Columbia, Canada. (include a note that the author's mother grew up in the Okanagan and I have been to see the monument by the lake many times)
- Mokele-Mbembe: Sauropod-like reptile rumored to inhabit the swamps of the Congo River Basin.
- Kraken: Colossal, tentacled sea monster capable of sinking ships, originating in Scandinavian folklore.
- Caddy (Cadborosaurus): Long, horse-headed sea serpent documented along the Pacific Coast of North America.
- Bessie: Serpentine lake monster reported in the eastern basins of Lake Erie, USA.
- Memphre: Reptilian lake creature sighted in Lake Memphremagog between Quebec, Canada, and Vermont.
- Steller's Sea Ape: Playful, unclassified marine mammal observed by naturalist Georg Steller in 1741.
- Lusca: Giant, predatory octopus-shark hybrid rumored to live in the deep blue holes of the Bahamas.
- Ningen: Colossal, white, humanoid marine entity reported by Japanese whale-research vessels in the Antarctic.

Winged Cryptids (Avian & Chiropteran):
- Mothman: Red-eyed, winged humanoid harbinger sighted before disasters, famously in Point Pleasant, West Virginia.
- Thunderbird: Massive, prehistoric-sized bird capable of creating thunder sounds, reported across North American skies.
- Ahool: Giant, predatory bat or flying reptile with a primate face, native to Java, Indonesia.
- Kongamato: Flying, tooth-billed pterosaur-like creature reported in the Jiundu swamps of Zambia.
- Ropen: Nocturnal, glowing flying reptile or pterosaur reported on Papua New Guinea islands.
- Jersey Devil: Kangaroo-bodied, bat-winged, horse-headed entity haunting the Pine Barrens of New Jersey.
- Owlman: Large, grey, owl-like humanoid sighted near the Mawnan church tower in Cornwall, England.
- Van Meter Monster: Winged, horn-headed entity that allegedly shot light beams in Iowa during 1903.
- Snallygaster: Bird-reptile hybrid with a metallic beak and tentacles, originating in Maryland folklore.

Terrestrial Mammals & Quadrupedal Predators:
- Chupacabra: Spikey, lizard-like or canine predator known for draining livestock blood, originating in Puerto Rico.
- Beast of Gévaudan: Massive, man-eating wolf-like terror that plagued south-central France in the 1760s.
- Queensland Tiger: Striped, cat-like marsupial predator reported in the rainforests of Queensland, Australia.
- Nandi Bear: Ferocious, nocturnal mammalian carnivore reported in the forested regions of East Africa.
- Shunka Warakin: Hyena-like mammal reported to kill livestock across the American state of Montana.
- Dingonek: Large, walrus-tusked, scale-armored mammalian predator rumored to patrol African jungle rivers.
- Gef the Talking Mongoose: High-intelligence, mongoose-like entity that allegedly haunted a farm on the Isle of Man.
- Ozark Howler: Bear-sized, dark-furred canine predator with thick horns, reported in the Ozark Mountains.
- Eastern Puma: Ghost-cat populations of cougars allegedly persisting in areas of eastern North America where declared extinct.

Serpentine & Draconic Reptiles:
- Hoop Snake: Serpent capable of biting its own tail to roll like a wheel after human prey.
- Tsuchinoko: Short, thick-bodied, venomous snake capable of jumping, native to the mountains of Japan.
- Mongolian Death Worm: Bright red, subterranean desert worm allegedly capable of spraying deadly acid or discharging electricity.
- Altamaha-ha: Sturgeon-like river monster with a snake body, native to the Altamaha River in Georgia, USA.
- Bunyip: Large, amphibious marsh-dweller with a dog-like face and horse tail from Australian Aboriginal mythology.
- Titanoboa Survivalists: Reports of modern, ultra-massive anacondas or pythons exceeding 50 feet in the Amazon Basin.

Anomalous Humanoids & Hybrids:
- Flatwoods Monster: Tall, hovering humanoid wearing a spade-shaped cowl, sighted in Flatwoods, West Virginia.
- Loveland Frogman: Four-foot-tall, bipedal frog creatures reported near the banks of the Little Miami River in Ohio.
- Lizard Man of Scape Ore Swamp: Seven-foot, green-scaled, three-toed bipedal reptilian reported in South Carolina.
- Popobawa: Shape-shifting, one-eyed bat humanoid that terrorizes residents of Zanzibar, Tanzania.
- Dover Demon: Pale, large-headed, thin-limbed humanoid sighted over a three-day period in Dover, Massachusetts.
- Goatman: Axe-wielding, half-man, half-goat hybrid creature originating from urban legends in Maryland and Texas.
- Fouke Monster: Red-eyed, aggressive, swamp-dwelling hominid made famous in Arkansas folklore.

